            <ArticleTitle>Identification of excessive back disability with the Faschingbauer Abbreviated MMPI.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>71-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Tested the accuracy of the MMPI and the FAM for predicting appropriate vs. inappropriate disability (illness behavior) in low back pain patients (N = 123). When the Hypochondriasis and Hysteria scales were used, both versions had a 79% hit rate for inappropriate disability and at least an 80% overall correct classification rate. The resulting brief screening measure included 52 items.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
